NOTICE
======

Capybara Map Editor is an independent, from-scratch Rust implementation of a
Diablo II DS1 map editor. It contains no code copied from the projects below,
but it owes them its understanding of the file formats and of how an editor
for them should behave.

Third-party licenses for everything in the exe: see THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md.


1. win_ds1edit by Paul Siramy (2002-2011)
-----------------------------------------

Paul Siramy wrote ds1edit / win_ds1edit, the DS1 map editor the Diablo II
modding community has relied on since 2002, and documented the DS1, DT1, DCC,
DC6, COF and AnimData.d2 formats for everyone.

    http://paul.siramy.free.fr/_divers/ds1/dl_ds1edit.html


2. DS1Edit by Ben Ethington (2025-2026), MIT License
----------------------------------------------------

DS1Edit (https://github.com/bethington/d2-ds1-edit) continues win_ds1edit. Its
format guides (docs/guides/*.md) were used as specifications, and its
headless renderer is used as a test oracle. It is not ported line by line.

Data files derived from DS1Edit and embedded in this program, if present,
are used under its MIT license:

    assets/editor/obj.txt     DS1 object -> COF token table
    assets/editor/ds1edit.dt1 editor marker tiles

